  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "MQTT (Message Queuing Telemetry Transport) is a lightweight publish-subscribe messaging protocol standardised as ISO/IEC 20922 and OASIS MQTT 5.0, designed for constrained devices and unreliable networks with minimal protocol overhead. Clients connect to a central broker that routes messages by topic; publishers post payloads to topic strings and subscribers receive all messages matching their subscribed topic filters. MQTT defines three quality-of-service levels\u2014at most once, at least once, and exactly once\u2014allowing integrators to balance message delivery guarantees against network and compute cost.",
